*Check (0)**.  It's the most sensible play given the context.\n\n\n", 'output': "Evaluation: You are in the Big Blind with Queen of Hearts and 10 of Hearts (QTs), which is a strong, playable hand with flush and straight potential. The opponent (Small Blind/Button) has just called (limped). You have the option to Check (0) and see the flop for free or Raise to take the initiative. Raising isolates the opponent and builds the pot, but playing a larger pot out of position can be risky. Checking allows you to realize your equity without investing more chips pre-flop, keeping the pot small and manageable, which aligns well with your current lead in the game standings.\n\nReason: Your hand (QTs) plays well post-flop. Since you are out of position and currently leading the overall match, the low-variance play is to Check. This allows you to see the community cards for free and avoids bloating the pot early when you don't have a made hand yet.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
