ckdoor flush draw, the King on the board connects well with the opponent's pre-flop calling range. Continuation betting here is risky because if you are called, you are likely behind, and if you are raised, you must fold. Checking allows you to keep the pot small, realize your equity by seeing a Turn card potentially for free, and re-evaluate if you hit an Ace or Queen.\n\nReason: Checking (0) is the prudent play to control pot size with Ace-high on a board that favors the opponent's range, while preserving the option to improve on the turn.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
